{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-hopf-structure-diagrams","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:hopf-structure-diagrams","kind":"remark","title":"Hopf-algebra structure: coassociativity","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-hopf-non-cocommutativity","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-self-dual-ses"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-quantum-observable-universe","tags":["hopf-algebra"],"text":"hopf-structure-diagrams.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<p><a id=\"rem:hopf-structure-diagrams\"></a>\n<strong>Remark.</strong> <em>Hopf-algebra structure: coassociativity</em></p>\n<p>The Hopf comultiplication <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Delta_q</code> on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{O}_q(\\mathrm{SU}(2))</code> obeys coassociativity.\nThis property is required for consistency across the theoretical framework.</p>\n"}
